    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0189" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Woodrow Wilson Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >House</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-28">October 28,
                            1918</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Much as I should enjoy Paris I think neutral place of meeting much wiser care
                    being taken not to choose a place where either German or English influence would
                    be strong. My preference is for Lausanne.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow
                                Wilson</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
